%% alt: Sequence diagram of starting JupyterLab. In the terminal you type jupyter lab inside the project folder. The terminal starts the Jupyter server in that folder. The server prints a URL that contains a token and opens it in the browser. The browser sends the token, and the server answers with the file browser of the folder where you started it. When you open a notebook and choose a kernel, the server launches that kernel, which is a separate Python process taken from the environment you picked. When you run a cell, the browser sends the code to the server, the server forwards it to the kernel, and the result travels back the same way.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor You
  participant T as Terminal
  participant S as Jupyter server
  participant B as Browser
  participant K as Kernel
  You->>T: `jupyter lab`
  T->>S: start in this folder
  S-->>T: URL with a token
  S->>B: open the URL
  B->>S: request plus token
  S-->>B: file browser of this folder
  You->>B: open a notebook, pick a kernel
  B->>S: start the kernel
  S->>K: launch that Python
  Note over S,K: the kernel is its own process
  You->>B: run a cell
  B->>S: code
  S->>K: code
  K-->>S: result
  S-->>B: result
